  - bounded lattice
  - counterexample
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Adams, Freese, Nation and Schmid proved that the complement of a maximal sublattice of a finite
  bounded lattice is an interval, and asked whether the same holds for finite semidistributive
  lattices; Adaricheva, Mata, Silberger and Zamojska-Dzienio conjectured that it does. It does not.
  In a 26-element semidistributive sublattice of the square of a 14-element semidistributive lattice,
  the diagonal is a maximal sublattice whose complement has two minimal elements. The proof is
  formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib.
